            "review_title": "Review at Jatujak Retro Bar",
            "review_text": "Veronica Morra\nDa Lat, Vietnam491 contributions\n0\nJatujak continues to be a little gem by Saigon Airport.\nJan 2024 • Solo\nI travel extensively and I always stay near the HCMC Airport, at Victory Airport Hotel. Several years ago I discovered a Thai Restaurant two blocks from the hotel and it has become my go to place.\nJATIJAK Retro Bar and restaurant. The food is Rhai and cagey always,accommodate my request fir \"khong cai\" or \"not spicy\". Though I like chilli, my system does not tolerate it well.\nSo, on my way to Indonesia and after a much needed nap, I headed over. My last time was mid November, on my way back from Croatia. I was surprised by all the new faces, though it is Tuesday and I am usually here on weekends. The menu also changed. The fabulous fried prawns,with onion rings, were not on the menu. Nonetheless, the fried chicken was fabulous. Tender boneles pieces iof crunchy outside and juicy inside, were so good I had to order seconds. The French fries needed salt, which was easily solved. The fried peanuts were hot and tasty, after I removed the slices of hot chilli. Their gin and tonic is the best I have had in Vietnam, very consistently excellent.The coconut ice cream with coconut gelatin, shaved coconut and peanuts was very flavorful. (I have had some with zero taste of coconut )\nSome of the staff I knew, who were not here, spoke relatively good English. That knowledge was absent tonight.\nMy only criticism is that every member of the staff walked around chewing food of some kind. I appreciate their right to feed themselves; but pretty much international standards are that eating or drinking while waiting on tables or in front of customers is in bad taste. \nI hope next time that mistake is not repeated.\nRead more\nWritten January 16, 2024",
